## Rebase SWRL builtin inference/materialization fixes (#171 / #172)
================================================================================

Context: Editor-generated SWRL rules with ``swrlb:`` builtins over datatype
properties still inferred zero triples on current 0.9.1 (issue #171). PR #172
was correct but targeted pre-``swrl/`` paths and conflicted with master.
Ported onto the topic package, kept the review follow-ups (IRI-safe
normalisation, shared ``partition_rule_atoms``, Postgres dialect gap
documented), and extracted ``SWRLSQLBuiltinFilters`` so ``SWRLSQLTranslator``
stays under the class size ceiling. Inference already emitted WHERE filters
(0.9.0); materialization, uri_map ``dataProperties``, registry prefixes, and
Lakebase ``TRY_CAST`` were still broken.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/reasoning/swrl/SWRLBuiltinRegistry.py
   Prefix- and IRI-tolerant ``_normalize`` for ``get`` / ``is_builtin``.
2. src/back/core/reasoning/swrl/SWRLEngine.py
   Fold class ``dataProperties`` into the uri_map (data namespace); object
   properties win a same-name clash, as in ``AggregateRuleEngine``.
3. src/back/core/reasoning/swrl/SWRLSQLTranslator.py
   ``dialect`` on the translator; inference/materialization reuse
   ``partition_rule_atoms``; builtins become WHERE filters and negated atoms
   ``NOT EXISTS``. Extract Method for filters, var-class map, and INSERT
   statements (size budget).
4. src/back/core/reasoning/swrl/SWRLSQLBuiltinFilters.py
   Extract Class: built-in SQL templates plus the Postgres
   ``TRY_CAST``/``DOUBLE`` rewrite (comparison/math only; remaining Lakebase
   gap documented).
5. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/LakebaseBase.py
   ``get_query_translator`` returns ``SWRLSQLTranslator(dialect="postgres")``.
6. tests/units/ontology/test_swrl_builtin_defects.py
   One regression class per defect (13 tests).
7. tests/units/architecture/baseline.json
   Drop ``build_materialization_sql`` (now under 100 LOC); shrink the other
   SWRL SQL builder entries.

