## Raise dependency security floors reported by Dependabot
================================================================================

Context: https://github.com/databrickslabs/ontobricks/security/dependabot
listed open alerts across Pillow, certifi, GitPython, mlflow, setuptools,
fastmcp/fastmcp-slim, opentelemetry-api, filelock, and black. Raised every
floor that has a published fix, citing the GHSA/Dependabot number next to
each pin, matching the existing constraint-dependencies convention. oauthlib
4.0.0 stays blocked (databricks-sql-connector 4.4–4.6 pins oauthlib<4.0.0,
already documented) and nltk has no patched release yet (already documented,
GHSA-8mgp-746c-j5xp).

IMPORTANT — uv.lock NOT regenerated: this sandbox has no network route to
the configured index (pypi-proxy.dev.databricks.com times out mid-TLS-
handshake; public PyPI unreachable too). `uv lock --offline` against the
local uv cache resolved but silently dropped Pillow from the lock and
jumped fastmcp 3.3.1 -> 4.1.3 and mcp 1.30.0 -> 2.3.0 (unvalidated major
versions) — rejected, not committed. These floor bumps in pyproject.toml do
NOT yet fix the alerts: Dependabot scans uv.lock, not pyproject.toml, and
`--frozen` test runs below still exercise the OLD pinned (vulnerable)
versions. Someone with working VPN/index access must run `uv lock` (root)
and `cd src/mcp-server && uv lock`, then `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not
scenario"` again, before this is actually fixed.

Changes:

1. pyproject.toml
   requires-python >=3.10 -> >=3.11 (pillow>=13.0.0 drops 3.10). Raised
   floors: mlflow>=3.17.2 (GHSA-2wqp-q3c6-ccj5, GHSA-wqmh-qccw-pqwf),
   black>=26.10.1 (GHSA-cg8m-r9f2-5wm2), fastmcp>=3.4.10
   (GHSA-7xgj-8392-5q4r), gitpython>=3.2.1 (GHSA-83vg-56qc-22m7),
   pillow>=13.0.0 (Dependabot #216-260), setuptools>=84.1.0
   (GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w). Added constraint-dependencies: certifi>=2026.10.19
   (GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2), filelock>=4.2.1 (GHSA-v4x8-3wr5-3wq8 and two
   more), fastmcp-slim>=3.4.10, opentelemetry-api>=1.45.1
   (GHSA-xcq7-p3pf-p88h).
2. src/mcp-server/pyproject.toml
   fastmcp>=2.3.1 -> >=3.4.10 (GHSA-7xgj-8392-5q4r). Added
   constraint-dependencies: certifi>=2026.10.19, fastmcp-slim>=3.4.10,
   opentelemetry-api>=1.45.1.

